  "description": "Artangel is presenting a new artwork in the Original Cell at Maughan Library which will be open to the public. The artwork is a sound piece, but requires a controlled and lowered light level in the space. We would therefore like to put removable double-sided blackout vinyl on the inside of the windows in that room, which will be visible from Chancery Lane. \n\nThe vinyl will be cut to fit inside each individual pane of glass so that the general aesthetic of the windows will remain the same both inside and externally. The vinyl will be applied to all six windows within one room of Maughan Library as indicated in our drawings. \n\nThe exhibition runs from 3rd July until 18th October 2026, with the vinyl in place from early June to late October 2026. The vinyl will be fully removable and will only be in place for approx 18-20 weeks. \n\nThe vinyl will NOT have any advertising on it, but might be a single colour on the street-facing side of the building. If the colour is an issue, we would consider it being a dark grey instead or black instead.  ",
